      "response": {
        "text": "Diagnosis:\n- The geo-service was experiencing a high error rate (34%) due to the upstream maps API returning 429 (Too Many Requests) errors.\n- Logs showed that the geo-cache service had an OOM event, evicted all keys, and became unavailable. As a result, geo-service bypassed the cache and sent all requests directly to the maps API, quickly exhausting the API quota.\n- Metrics confirmed the cache hit ratio dropped to zero during the incident, and maps API call volume spiked.\n\nRemediation:\n- I restarted the geo-cache service to recover it from the OOM state.\n- After the restart, the cache hit ratio recovered (now at 0.88), and the geo-service error rate dropped back to normal (0.4%).\n\nSummary:\n- The issue was caused by a failed geo-cache, leading to API quota exhaustion.\n- Restarting geo-cache restored normal operation and resolved the alert. No further action is needed at this time.",
